Hey Kevin,

If you want to be able to compare SPL from different recordings, different studies and different pieces of equipment, I don't see any other option than hardware calibration, that is with a calibrator at the moment you are taking the recording. All the calculations in the world won't get around it i'm afraid. This is because the amplitude will always be relative in the recording. You can also measure the SPL with a calibrated SPLmeter and then calculate the SPL values for the sounds you recorded.

Hope this helped!
Best
Sandra.

