Hey Sandra :)

Actually, I mentioned the paper (Merchant et al. 2015) whose methodology
I am using to calibrate my SPL values in the first post.

Although the end-to-end calibration that you suggest is preferred, we
can get rough calibrated SPL measurements using the manufacturer's
specifications (mic sensitivity, gain, ADC voltage). I separately
measured relative microphone sensitivities additionally as I found that
they are most variable.

I use Song Meters and these technical data are available to calculate a
correction term that I will subtract from the uncorrected SPL values
that I hope to get from meanspec(). It's just that I'm unsure about
meanspec's output.

